{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018SoibWEX8bkxP4Ub8coKXx","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/TODO.md:19:- #50 Scanner: missing-tests\ndocs/TODO.md:24:- #213 Scanner: missing-tests, part 2: scan, Dockerfile and starter wiring\ndocs/proposal.md:215:| missing-tests | coverage report plus exported functions with no test | 24 h | 10 per package | yes |\n\n**The stale closer is a built-in scanner.** It has no role directory and needs no job slot, executor or worktree; its settings live in the top-level `stale:` block of `config.yaml`. It is a plain cont\n\n| Scanner | Engine | Every | Group size | Auto-close |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| cve | osv-scanner and govulncheck (trivy and the Dependabot alerts API later) | 6 h | 1 | yes |\n| lts | endoflife.date + manifests: go.mod, package.json, Dockerfile `FROM`, Helm charts | 7 d | 1 per component | yes |\n| lint | repo linters, findings beyond a committed baseline | 24 h | 20 per rule and directory | yes |\n| error-codes | pattern match over source, registry and docs files (`sh` + `jq`) | 24 h | 20 | yes |\n| trufflehog | leaked-credential scan of the current commit (`sh` + `jq` + TruffleHog) | 24 h | 1 | yes |\n| missing-tests | coverage report plus exported functions with no test | 24 h | 10 per package | yes |\n| docs | undocumented exported Go identifiers and package comments (deterministic) | 3 d | 10 per package | yes |\n| docs-drift | LLM: docs that contradict the code (planned; needs the LLM scanner engine, #204) | 3 d | 10 per doc file | no |\n| architecture | LLM against ADRs and the sidecar spec repo | 3 d | 1 | no |\n| stale | built-in | 24 h | none | none |\n\n**The cve scanner** (`scanners/cve`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program, no build step) merges osv-scanner (all ecosystems) and govulncheck (Go reachability). Its fingerprint is `osv:<advisory>:<mani\n\n\nsidecars:\n  vpe-specs: { repo: <owner>/specs, ref: main }   # ref: branch, tag or full 40-hex SHA; default main\n\noverrides:                   # only what differs from convention\n  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/docs:            { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes:     { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/trufflehog:      { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n  scanners/lint:            { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:              { sidecar: vpe-specs, timeout: 15m, model: claude-opus-5-5 }\n1://go:build ignore\n7:// carries the ignore build tag, so go vet ./... and go build ./... skip it.\n121:\tvar packages, profile, ignore string\n128:\tfs.StringVar(&ignore, \"ignore\", \"\", \"optional ignore file\")\n155:\tif ignore != \"\" {\n156:\t\tif rules, err = readIgnore(ignore); err != nil {\n194:\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, \"missing-tests: warning: ignore pattern %q matches nothing\\n\", r.raw)\n198:\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"too many findings (%d, limit %d): add an ignore file or no-coverage\", len(found), cfg.max)\n442:// readIgnore reads the optional ignore file. A malformed line is an error.\n443:func readIgnore(file string) ([]ignoreRule, error) {\n17:func TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n32:\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\", \"scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"triage/architect/prompt.txt\", \"triage/designer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/documentation-planner/prompt.txt\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"triage/product-manager/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n45:func TestScanIsExecutableOnDisk(t *testing.T) {\n46:\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\"} {\n57:func TestExecutableNames(t *testing.T) {\n65:func TestEmbeddedCveRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n98:func TestEmbeddedErrorCodesRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n121:func TestEmbeddedDocsRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n172:func TestEmbeddedTrufflehogRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n178:\t\tif r.Kind != config.KindScanner || r.Name != \"trufflehog\" {\n181:\t\tif r.ScanPath != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\" || !r.Autoclose || r.Every != 24*time.Hour || r.GroupSize != 1 || r.MaxOpen != 5 || r.Timeout != 30*time.Minute {\n187:\t\tif r.Dockerfile != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\" {\n195:\tt.Fatal(\"no scanner role trufflehog\")\ngo.mod\nmain.go\np\nwant.jsonl\n34:func thResultLine(raw, det, file string, line int) thLine {\n42:func thSummary(chunks, unverified int) string {\n47:func thJoin(lines []thLine) string {\n58:func thRun(t *testing.T, out, errlog string, rc int, files map[string]string, extra map[string]string) thResult {\n63:func thRunWith(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int) thResult {\n68:func thRunFull(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int, files map[string]string, extra map[string]string) thResult {\n119:func thTmpEmpty(t *testing.T, tmp string) {\n126:func TestTrufflehogAggregatesAndFingerprints(t *testing.T) {\n177:func TestTrufflehogFailsClosed(t *testing.T) {\n238:func thRunRole(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int) thResult {\n243:func TestTrufflehogArgvAndExcludes(t *testing.T) {\n260:func TestTrufflehogMissingTool(t *testing.T) {\n273:func TestTrufflehogDockerfilePins(t *testing.T) {\n297:func TestTrufflehogAllow(t *testing.T) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afee17e5-2dea-4ea0-9380-6eb29683278d","uuid":"5e2da2f6-8b43-4846-9dc9-d96cc427605f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:13:43.453Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/TODO.md:19:- #50 Scanner: missing-tests\ndocs/TODO.md:24:- #213 Scanner: missing-tests, part 2: scan, Dockerfile and starter wiring\ndocs/proposal.md:215:| missing-tests | coverage report plus exported functions with no test | 24 h | 10 per package | yes |\n\n**The stale closer is a built-in scanner.** It has no role directory and needs no job slot, executor or worktree; its settings live in the top-level `stale:` block of `config.yaml`. It is a plain cont\n\n| Scanner | Engine | Every | Group size | Auto-close |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| cve | osv-scanner and govulncheck (trivy and the Dependabot alerts API later) | 6 h | 1 | yes |\n| lts | endoflife.date + manifests: go.mod, package.json, Dockerfile `FROM`, Helm charts | 7 d | 1 per component | yes |\n| lint | repo linters, findings beyond a committed baseline | 24 h | 20 per rule and directory | yes |\n| error-codes | pattern match over source, registry and docs files (`sh` + `jq`) | 24 h | 20 | yes |\n| trufflehog | leaked-credential scan of the current commit (`sh` + `jq` + TruffleHog) | 24 h | 1 | yes |\n| missing-tests | coverage report plus exported functions with no test | 24 h | 10 per package | yes |\n| docs | undocumented exported Go identifiers and package comments (deterministic) | 3 d | 10 per package | yes |\n| docs-drift | LLM: docs that contradict the code (planned; needs the LLM scanner engine, #204) | 3 d | 10 per doc file | no |\n| architecture | LLM against ADRs and the sidecar spec repo | 3 d | 1 | no |\n| stale | built-in | 24 h | none | none |\n\n**The cve scanner** (`scanners/cve`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program, no build step) merges osv-scanner (all ecosystems) and govulncheck (Go reachability). Its fingerprint is `osv:<advisory>: